    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23Yd38q22bNvkAAYUumjJrU)_\n\n**Before:** the mode line showed no buffer name, no major or minor mode, nothing. `sp-lambda-line` (the module `init.el` loads; there is no `sp-modeline.el` on `main`) calls `(lambda-line-mode)`, which with `lambda-line-position` `bottom` puts the status line in `mode-line-format`. The next form then set `mode-line-format` to a bare `\"%_\"` when the position is `bottom`, overwriting it. That divider trick is only for `top`, where the status line lives in the header line (it was `'top` in `sp-choose-modeline`). Separately, lambda-line's default format never shows minor modes (symbol, buffer name, major mode + branch, position, time).\n\n**After:**\n- `sp-lambda-line`: the divider is set only for `top`, so the status line shows (buffer name, major mode, branch, position).\n- New `sp-modeline` (tooling), adapted from `prot-modeline.el` and `prot-emacs-modeline.el`: no `prot-common`/`prot-icons` and no package, faces inherit from the theme (no hard-coded hex colours), plus minor modes (`sp-modeline-minor-modes-style`: lighters, count or nil), and `global-mode-string` so `sp-tag-emoji` shows. Not loaded by `init.el`; a commented `'sp-modeline` sits beside `'sp-lambda-line` in both lists (load one of the two).\n- Doc `docs/tangles/tooling/sp-modeline.org` tangles to the `.el`; `sp-lambda-line.org`, `main.org` and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run (no Emacs in the container; the `.el` was only paren-balanced by script). Check in your Emacs 31 that the lambda-line fix shows the line, and try `sp-modeline` with `M-x sp-modeline-mode` after `(require 'sp-modeline)`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
